      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186129154/plots/60307bff7162ad99e2908e391903d4fb6c2f11e35964a1c13f3d5ed581c32b07.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$\n- **II.** $p(0)=0.$\n- **III.** $x=3$ is a root of even multiplicity.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As $x$ moves left in the negative direction towards $-\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=0$, which means that $p(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The root $x=3$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e31a70f0-0026-5787-93be-68232d3eb873",
